James, Luciano,

Thanks for your almost identical solutions - I did not know about the
melt function! They worked beautifully with my simple example. I've
attempted to apply the same approach to my larger/slightly more
complex data set. It almost works, except the 1st parameter
("Interacts with other organisms") is not plotted:
http://people.brandeis.edu/~dcaffrey/tmp/myplot.pdf

and I get the following warnings which are perhaps related.

Warning messages:
1: Removed 65 rows containing missing values (stat_density).
2: Removed 32 rows containing missing values (stat_density).
3: Removed 65 rows containing missing values (stat_density).
4: Removed 1158 rows containing missing values (stat_density).

I suspect that this might have something to do with the contents of my
melted data.frame but I'm not sure how to debug it and I could not
find missing values when using is.na <http://is.na>(). The slightly more complicated
code is below.

Thanks again and I apologize if I have missed something that should be
obvious.

Daniel

library(ggplot2)
preferredName <- c("Interacts with other organisms","Response to other
organism","All gene sets","Rest of genome")

#get the data I want
data <- read.csv(file="http://people.brandeis.edu/~dcaffrey/tmp/
variations2.csv",header=TRUE,stringsAsFactor=FALSE,comment.char =
"#")columnsWithGo <- grep ("hasGoTerm",names(data))
names(data)[columnsWithGo] <- preferredName[1:
(length(preferredName)-2)]
rowsWithAnyGo <- which (data[,columnsWithGo]==TRUE,arr.ind=TRUE)
rowsWithAnyGo <- unique(rowsWithAnyGo[,1])
anyGo <- rep(FALSE,dim(data)[1])
anyGo[rowsWithAnyGo] <- TRUE
noGo <- rep(TRUE,dim(data)[1])
noGo[rowsWithAnyGo] <- FALSE
numColumns <-  dim(data)[2]
#only need certain columns
combinedDf <- cbind(data[,c(10,columnsWithGo)],anyGo,noGo)

#melt
meltedDf <- melt(combinedDf,id="nsNormBySize")
meltedDf <- meltedDf[meltedDf$value,]

#plot
p <- ggplot( meltedDf, aes(x=nsNormBySize,color=variable) ) +
geom_density(linetype=2)

p <- p + scale_x_continuous('Non-synonymous polymorphisms / CD

length',limits=c(0,0.01))

p <- p + scale_y_continuous( 'Density',limits=c(0,300))

# next line causes error relating to length
#p <- p + scale_colour_manual("Gene sets", breaks = levels(meltedDf
$variable), labels = preferredName)

print(p)
ggsave("myPlot.pdf", p)

