Subject: Error: attempt to apply non-function
Message-ID: <p4buZUH8BNQ.F_VWcc4r6z0J@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/p4buZUH8BNQ/m/F_VWcc4r6z0J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

below an example of a qplot failure when seq is the name of a variable
in the calling environment. I would consider this a nuisance, maybe
even a bug. Maybe it is related to the use of parent.frame() in
qqplot?

Cheers,
Jochen

library(ggplot2)
x <- -10:10
y <- sin(x)
s <- data.frame(x=x, y=y)
qplot(x=x, y=y, data=s)
# works

seq <- s
qplot(x=x, y=y, data=s)
# Error in get(x, envir = this, inherits = inh)(this, ...) :
#  attempt to apply non-function

rm(seq)
qplot(x=x, y=y, data=s)
# works again

